I come out of the clinic.
There is a medical store near my building, I go there.
The doctor's prescription is in my hand.
There is still a severe pain in my head, and pain in my throat too.
I go inside the medical store.
A man is standing at the counter there.
I say, "Bhaiya, namaste."
I give the doctor's prescription to him.
He reads the prescription and nods his head.
He says, "Madam, please wait one minute."
He brings some tablets and one bottle of cough syrup.
He says, "These tablets are for three days."
"And drink this cough medicine twice a day."
I say, "Alright, how many rupees for this?"
He says, "Two hundred and fifty rupees."
I give him the money.
He places the medicines in a small bag.
He says, "Take the medicine, you should rest well now."
I say thank you, take the bag, and go towards home.
